[{"text":"CSP[p, q] is the 3-dimensional scalar product of p with q and is transformed into CartesianPair[CartesianMomentum[p],CartesianMomentum[q]] by FeynCalcInternal.","anchor":"csp"},{"text":"CSP[p] is the same as CSP[p,p] (=p^2).","anchor":"csp"},{"text":"Overview, SP, ScalarProduct, CartesianScalarProduct.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"CSP[p, q] + CSP[q]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}+\\overline{q}^2\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSP[p - q, q + 2 p]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q})\\cdot (2 \\overline{p}+\\overline{q})\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Calc[ CSP[p - q, q + 2 p] ]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}+2 \\overline{p}^2-\\overline{q}^2\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ExpandScalarProduct[CSP[p - q]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-2 \\left(\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)+\\overline{p}^2+\\overline{q}^2\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSP[a, b] // StandardForm (*CSP[a, b]*)","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSP[a, b] // FCI // StandardForm (*CartesianPair[CartesianMomentum[a], CartesianMomentum[b]]*)","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CSP[a, b] // FCI // FCE // StandardForm (*CSP[a, b]*)","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"}]